{"term":"spill","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ae511a481ef5e6c4d4","definition":"To drop something so that it spreads out or makes a mess; to accidentally pour.","example":"I spilled some sticky juice on the kitchen floor.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d9ebf5e2820c765de3","definition":"To spread out or fall out, as above.","example":"Some sticky juice spilled onto the kitchen floor.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0c0e8c3898b1672b34","definition":"To overflow out of a designated area.","example":"The crowd spilled onto Maple Avenue.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e007535e16336b7e87","definition":"To drop something that was intended to be caught.","example":"That should have been that, but Hart caught a dose of the Hennessey wobbles and spilled Adlene Guedioura's long-range shot.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1bb632f8d6a0dd3fb","definition":"To mar; to damage; to destroy by misuse; to waste.","example":"They [the colours] disfigure the stuff and spill the whole workmanship.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f0eda5e1322a602c5","definition":"To be destroyed, ruined, or wasted; to come to ruin; to perish; to waste.","example":"That thou wilt suffer innocence to spill.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:399b970b2fcb13f1fa","definition":"To overflow or flow out, over or off something.","example":"Liverpool Street's 1985-92 remodelling by the British Rail Architects' Department (under project lead Nick Derbyshire) had carefully followed original 1870s detailing, with the concourse designed to allow natural light to spill into the station.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:27851d5d7a6af81432","definition":"To cause or flow out and be lost or wasted; to shed.","example":"to revenge his Blood, ſo juſtly ſpilt, / VVhat is it leſs then to partake his guilt?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:02fcfbae6a9d922943","definition":"To cause to be thrown from a mount, a carriage, etc.","example":"Then, not thirty feet beyond, a sudden panicky lunge to the side by his horse spilled him from the saddle.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, slang","register":"obsolete, slang, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ae25dd3569dfaff9a","definition":"To cover or decorate with slender pieces of wood, metal, ivory, etc.; to inlay.","example":"And all the others pavement were with yvory spilt","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:47ceb0916bc109c52f","definition":"To relieve a sail from the pressure of the wind, so that it can be more easily reefed or furled, or to lessen the strain.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1ae254b048377ea28","definition":"To open the leadership of a parliamentary party for re-election.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Australian","register":"Australian, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35796b79e37d45d9ad","definition":"To reveal information to an uninfo